Title => Every Type Once
Syntax => 3
Languages => en | nl

## Masks and media

Question => Which photo shows the **moon**?
Media => moon.jpg { alt="The moon, up close", credit="NASA", fit=cover }
Answers => ?moon.jpg | earth.jpg
Type => Choice
Correct => moon.jpg
FormatText => false

Question => Name the three colours in the flag.
Answers =>
Red
White
Blue
Type => List
Correct => Red | White | Blue
Scoring => partial
AlsoAccept => Rouge
Reject => Purple

Question => Sort these from smallest to largest.
Answers => Ant | Dog | Whale
Type => Sort
AnswersOrder => shuffle

Question => A tiny poem about printers.
Answers => Paper jam
Class => spotlight | center
Layout => media-left
Background => color:#101820
Print => no-background
Transition => fade
Direction => ltr

Question => Where is the lighthouse?
Media => map.png { alt="A coastline map" }
Answers => 30,40
Type => Hotspot
HitRadius => 6

Question => Rank the albums.
Answers => First | Second | Third
Type => Rank

Question => How far away is the moon?
Answers => 384400
Type => Estimate
Tolerance => 500
Unit => km
Slider => 380000..390000

Question => Which one is not a planet?
Answers => Mars | Venus | Pluto
Type => OddOneOut
Correct => Pluto
AlsoAccept => pluto is a dwarf planet

Question => Mark each claim.
Answers => True | False
Rows => The sky is blue | Water is dry
Correct => True | False

Question => Name the band and the singer.
Type => Parts
Parts => open: Band: 2 | open: Singer: 1
Answers => The Beatles || Paul McCartney

Question => Put these in the right bucket.
Type => Classification
Answers => Apple | Carrot
Buckets => Fruit | Vegetable
Correct => Apple @ Fruit | Carrot @ Vegetable

Question => Label the parts.
Type => Diagram
Media => map.png { alt="A diagram of a door" }
Answers => Handle | Hinge
Targets => Handle spot @ 30,50 | Hinge spot @ 70,50
Correct => Handle @ Handle spot | Hinge @ Hinge spot

Question => Which planet is the odd one out?
Answers => Mars | Venus | Pluto
Type => Choice
Correct => Mars | Venus
Negate => true
Feedback => A rocky neighbour. | Also a rocky neighbour. | Not a planet any more.
Wager => true
Buzzer => true

Question => Which year did the moon landing happen?
Answers => 1969
Type => Range
Range => 0
Slider => 1900..2000
Suggest => 1969 | 1968
PlayLimit => 1
